;; Live conformance for the kura shard-store contract, run inside a Cloudflare
;; Worker against a real R2 bucket.
;;
;; It exists because two bugs got past the unit suite in a row, both of the
;; same shape: a test that supplies its own world agrees with itself.
;;   1. the synchronous IShardStore protocol silently reported every read as
;;      absent when handed an async transport — FakeHttp in the tests is
;;      synchronous, so the tests were self-consistent and wrong together;
;;   2. an un-inferred property read (.-objects) is renamed by :advanced and
;;      returns undefined — no unit test runs through :advanced.
;; Only a suite that runs the real code against a real object store finds
;; either one.
;;
;; Library deps are shadow source-paths from the west checkout (sibling
;; layout), the pattern kotobase-protocols-worker uses.
{:source-paths
 ["src"
  "../kura-node/src"
  "../kura/src"
  "../erasure/src"
  "../merkle-sum/src"
  "../sigv4/src"]
 :dependencies []
 :builds
 {:worker {:target :esm
           :output-dir "out"
           ;; Serialize: parallel par-compile aborts under CPU contention from
           ;; concurrent agent builds on this machine.
           :compiler-options {:parallel-build false}
           :modules {:worker {:exports {default kura.conformance.worker/handler}}}}}}
